&lt;p&gt;As Director of Platform Engineering at SingleStore, you will lead the teams and technologies that power the company’s internal engineering platforms, infrastructure services, and developer experience. You will be responsible for building and operating the systems that enable engineers to develop, test, secure, deploy, and operate software reliably at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role owns critical platform domains including CI/CD infrastructure, release engineering, developer productivity tooling, infrastructure automation, identity and access management, networking infrastructure, observability, and internal cloud platforms. You will drive operational excellence across multi-cloud environments while improving reliability, scalability, security, and engineering velocity across the organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own the strategy, standardization, and operational maturity of SingleStore’s internal multi-cloud infrastructure services environment. This includes driving consistency, automation, scalability, and operational best practices across cloud service providers while ensuring critical engineering systems remain secure, reliable, and operationally efficient.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will partner closely with Engineering, Security, IT, and Product leadership to modernize platform capabilities, standardize engineering workflows, and scale the infrastructure that supports SingleStore’s cloud and database engineering teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By combining deep expertise in platform engineering, infrastructure operations, multi-cloud architecture, networking, IAM, and developer systems, you will shape how engineering teams build, deploy, and operate software across the company. In addition, you will champion AI- and automation-driven approaches to modernize infrastructure operations, release pipelines, and developer tooling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is a deeply technical engineering leader with experience building and operating large-scale platform and infrastructure systems. You are equally comfortable driving long-term platform strategy, mentoring engineering teams, and engaging directly with architecture, operational challenges, and infrastructure modernization efforts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platform Engineering Leadership - &lt;/strong&gt;Lead the Platform Engineering organization responsible for developer infrastructure, CI/CD systems, release engineering, internal cloud platforms, infrastructure automation, and engineering productivity tooling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Infrastructure &amp;amp; Core Services Ownership&lt;/strong&gt; - Own and operate core infrastructure services including identity and access management (Keycloak, FreeIPA), VPN and secure remote access systems, NetBox/IPAM, internal DNS, and cloud networking infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Developer Platforms &amp;amp; CI/CD - &lt;/strong&gt;Drive the evolution of scalable developer platforms and CI/CD systems that improve engineering velocity, build reliability, deployment safety, and operational consistency across distributed teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Infrastructure Automation&lt;/strong&gt; - Champion infrastructure-as-code, automation frameworks, and AI-assisted operational tooling to reduce operational overhead and improve platform scalability and reliability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reliability &amp;amp; Operational Excellence&lt;/strong&gt; - Establish best practices for observability, incident response, capacity planning, security, platform reliability, and infrastructure lifecycle management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Engineering Leadership&lt;/strong&gt; - Partner with Engineering, Security, SRE, and IT leadership to align platform capabilities with organizational priorities and deliver scalable engineering infrastructure solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership &amp;amp; Mentorship&lt;/strong&gt; - Build, mentor, and grow high-performing platform and infrastructure engineering teams while fostering a culture of ownership, technical excellence, and continuous improvement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Platform Roadmap&lt;/strong&gt; - Define and execute the long-term roadmap for internal engineering platforms, infrastructure modernization, developer experience, and operational tooling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Requirements&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in Platform Engineering, Infrastructure Engineering, DevOps, SRE, or related technical disciplines, including 5+ years leading engineering or infrastructure organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience designing, operating, and scaling internal engineering platforms and infrastructure services in complex multi-cloud environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical expertise across:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multi-cloud infrastructure (AWS, GCP, Azure)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CI/CD and release engineering systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Infrastructure automation and Infrastructure-as-Code (Terraform, Ansible, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Linux systems administration and networking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Observability, monitoring, and operational tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identity and access management systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building standardized and automated infrastructure platforms across multiple cloud service providers, including establishing consistent operational patterns, tooling, security controls, and deployment workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on operational experience managing and scaling critical infrastructure services including:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keycloak&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;FreeIPA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;VPN and secure remote access infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;NetBox/IPAM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;DNS, PKI, and internal networking systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of infrastructure lifecycle management, operational processes, system reliability, and engineering scalability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to build and mature operational processes that improve reliability, security, scalability, and engineering efficiency across distributed environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to remain technically engaged while leading teams, driving architectural decisions, troubleshooting complex infrastructure challenges, and mentoring engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong process orientation with experience building repeatable, scalable operational frameworks and engineering standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to align infrastructure strategy with engineering and business priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading Platform Engineering or Internal Developer Platform organizations in high-growth cloud-native or infrastructure-focused companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Kubernetes, Terraform, GitHub Actions, ArgoCD, or similar cloud-native infrastructure tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with SRE practices including SLIs/SLOs, incident management, and production operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing AI-assisted automation in infrastructure operations, developer tooling, or CI/CD systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Python, Go, or scripting languages used for infrastructure automation and operational tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing globally distributed infrastructure and engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cloud architecture or infrastructure certifications (AWS/GCP/Azure).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Excited about joining the SingleStore team, but don&#39;t see a position that matches your background?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;d still love to hear from you through this application!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re growing fast and if your background matches a new opportunity, we will&amp;nbsp;gladly reach out.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;SingleStore is one platform for all data, built so you can engage with insight in every moment. Trusted by industry leaders, SingleStore enables enterprises to adapt to change as it happens, embrace diverse data with ease, and accelerate the pace of innovation. SingleStore is venture-backed and headquartered in San Francisco with offices in Portland, Seattle, Boston, Bangalore, London, Lisbon, and Kyiv. Defining the future starts with The Database of Now™.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Consistent with our commitment to diversity &amp;amp; inclusion, we value individuals with the ability to work on diverse teams and with a diverse range of people.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;To all recruitment agencies: SingleStore does not accept agency resumes. Please do not forward resumes to SingleStore employees. SingleStore is not responsible for any fees related to unsolicited resumes and will not pay fees to any third-party agency or company that does not have a signed agreement with the Company.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p data-start=&quot;0&quot; data-end=&quot;247&quot;&gt;Interested in future Engineering opportunities with SingleStore? Join our Engineering Talent Community and stay connected with upcoming openings across our Product, Engineering, and Infrastructure teams in the United States, EMEA, and global hubs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;249&quot; data-end=&quot;460&quot;&gt;We’re always interested in speaking with talented engineers who are passionate about building high-performance systems, solving complex technical challenges, and shaping the future of data and AI infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;462&quot; data-end=&quot;529&quot;&gt;We’d love to hear from candidates with experience in areas such as:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;531&quot; data-end=&quot;783&quot;&gt;Software Engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;531&quot; data-end=&quot;783&quot;&gt;Distributed Systems Engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;531&quot; data-end=&quot;783&quot;&gt;Database Engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;531&quot; data-end=&quot;783&quot;&gt;Site Reliability Engineers (SRE)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;531&quot; data-end=&quot;783&quot;&gt;Cloud / Private Cloud Engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;531&quot; data-end=&quot;783&quot;&gt;Performance Engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;531&quot; data-end=&quot;783&quot;&gt;Backend Engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;531&quot; data-end=&quot;783&quot;&gt;AI / ML Infrastructure Engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;531&quot; data-end=&quot;783&quot;&gt;Interns and New Grad Engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;785&quot; data-end=&quot;1013&quot;&gt;At SingleStore, our Engineering teams build the technology powering some of the world’s most innovative companies, enabling real-time analytics, scalable applications, and next-generation AI workloads on a unified data platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 data-section-id=&quot;vo0ejc&quot; data-start=&quot;1015&quot; data-end=&quot;1040&quot;&gt;Why Join SingleStore?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;1041&quot; data-end=&quot;1398&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1tz31h5&quot; data-start=&quot;1041&quot; data-end=&quot;1107&quot;&gt;High-growth company at the forefront of data and AI innovation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;q4w48l&quot; data-start=&quot;1108&quot; data-end=&quot;1194&quot;&gt;Opportunities across core database, cloud, infrastructure, and product engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;hsog57&quot; data-start=&quot;1195&quot; data-end=&quot;1262&quot;&gt;Global, collaborative, and high-performance engineering culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;u79iop&quot; data-start=&quot;1263&quot; data-end=&quot;1327&quot;&gt;Meaningful technical challenges with visible customer impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;rmkh6m&quot; data-start=&quot;1328&quot; data-end=&quot;1398&quot;&gt;Ability to work on systems built for speed, scale, and reliability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 data-section-id=&quot;1xmjzt&quot; data-start=&quot;1400&quot; data-end=&quot;1429&quot;&gt;Join Our Talent Community&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1430&quot; data-end=&quot;1659&quot;&gt;If you’re interested in being considered for future opportunities, submit your profile to our Engineering Talent Community. Our Talent team will review your background and reach out when relevant roles align with your experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1661&quot; data-end=&quot;1700&quot; data-is-last-node=&quot;&quot; data-is-only-node=&quot;&quot;&gt;We look forward to connecting with you.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;SingleStore is seeking an accomplished sales professional to join our Enterprise Sales Team. In this role, you will be responsible for closing new business and expanding existing relationships with large enterprise customers, leading complex sales cycles and navigating multi-stakeholder buying environments. You will develop and maintain senior-level customer relationships and apply a value-selling approach that connects SingleStore’s technology to measurable business outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Enterprise Account Executives at SingleStore are strategic, customer-focused sellers who are passionate about evangelizing modern data infrastructure solutions. You bring a strong understanding of the enterprise market landscape, collaborate closely with Sales Engineering and Sales Development, and are able to clearly articulate solution value to both technical and business stakeholders within large, complex organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role and Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute territory and account plans to consistently achieve revenue targets within a defined portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead multiple, concurrent customer sales cycles end to end, with a strong focus on new logo acquisition while managing longer, more complex deal timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and grow large, enterprise customer accounts, navigating multi-stakeholder environments and managing complexity across decision-makers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Sales Engineering, Sales Development, and Field Marketing to drive deal strategy, pipeline generation, and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain relationships with Channel partners, supporting pipeline development and co-selling efforts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quickly develop a deep understanding of the company’s software products and clearly articulate the business value to both technical and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop strong relationships with key decision-makers, influencers, and partners within your territory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and maintain strong relationships with key decision-makers, influencers, and partners across assigned accounts and territory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel within the assigned territory as required to support customer engagement and sales activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5-10 yrs of proven track record of successfully selling enterprise software solutions and increasing revenue through new customer acquisition&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solution selling of a disruptive technology in the data infrastructure space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Firm understanding of the modern data infrastructure such as the open source community and the various enterprise software (business intelligence, analytics, ETL, cloud infrastructure, etc.) products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to sell to CXO or line of business, successfully emphasizing business value versus product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ability to connect with customers to understand their individual business needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.A, B.S. degree or equivalent in a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SingleStore delivers the cloud-native database with the speed and scale to power the world’s data-intensive applications. With a distributed SQL database that introduces simplicity to your data architecture by unifying transactions and analytics, SingleStore empowers digital leaders to deliver exceptional, real-time data experiences to their customers. SingleStore is venture-backed and headquartered in San Francisco with offices in Sunnyvale, Raleigh, Seattle, Boston, London, Lisbon, Bangalore, Dublin and Kyiv.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Consistent with our commitment to diversity &amp;amp; inclusion, we value individuals with the ability to work on diverse teams and with a diverse range of people.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;To all recruitment agencies: SingleStore does not accept agency resumes. Please do not forward resumes to SingleStore employees. SingleStore is not responsible for any fees related to unsolicited resumes and will not pay fees to any third-party agency or company that does not have a signed agreement with the Company.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SingleStore values individuals for their unique skills and experiences, and we’re proud to offer roles in a variety of locations across the United States. Salary is based on permissible, non-discriminatory factors such as skills, experience, and geographic location, and is just one part of our total compensation and benefits package. Certain roles are also eligible for additional rewards, including merit increases and annual bonuses.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SingleStore’s base salary range for this role, if based in Boston, Chicago, New York, Austin, Phoenix, Las Vegas, Seattle, Washington, or Dallas is: $120,000 -&amp;nbsp; $175,000 USD per year&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;For candidates residing in California, please see our&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.singlestore.com/singlestore-california-recruitment-privacy-notice/&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt; California Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;. For candidates residing in the EEA, UK, and Switzerland, please see our&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.singlestore.com/recruitment-privacy/&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt; EEA, UK, and Swiss Recruitment Privacy Notice.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Assistant&lt;/strong&gt; to C-Suite&lt;br&gt;The Executive Assistant to the C-Suite is a trusted strategic partner who helps leadership operate at maximum effectiveness. This role goes beyond traditional administrative support and requires exceptional judgment, discretion, anticipation, and the ability to manage complexity with precision. The ideal candidate thrives in a fast-paced, high-growth environment and brings a builder mindset, strong ownership, and a desire to make an impact. C-suite executive assistant roles typically center on high-level calendar management, communications, travel, and project coordination.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to SingleStore’s leaders, this role will support a broad range of responsibilities, including executive calendar and travel management, internal and external communications, event coordination, and select project management. You will work closely with senior leaders, direct reports, and external stakeholders to help drive the rhythm and execution of key priorities. Effective executive support in this setting depends on proactive coordination, clear communication, and the ability to anticipate needs before they arise. This role is best suited for someone who can operate as a true partner to leadership, not just an administrator. The strongest candidates will be calm under pressure, polished with stakeholders, and confident handling both business-critical and sensitive support needs, while balancing structure with flexibility in a collaborative environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of professional experience, ideally supporting a C-level executive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational skills and attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple priorities in a dynamic environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills and comfort navigating ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High discretion and comfort handling confidential information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership mindset with a proactive, adaptable, and solutions-oriented approach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Google Workspace and GSuite&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability and willingness to work onsite two days per week or as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SingleStore delivers the cloud-native database with the speed and scale to power the world’s data-intensive applications. With a distributed SQL database that introduces simplicity to your data architecture by unifying transactions and analytics, SingleStore empowers digital leaders to deliver exceptional, real-time data experiences to their customers. SingleStore is venture-backed and headquartered in San Francisco with offices in Raleigh, Seattle, Boston, London, Lisbon, Bangalore, Dublin and Kyiv.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Consistent with our commitment to diversity &amp;amp; inclusion, we value individuals with the ability to work on diverse teams and with a diverse range of people.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;To all recruitment agencies: SingleStore does not accept agency resumes. Please do not forward resumes to SingleStore employees. SingleStore is not responsible for any fees related to unsolicited resumes and will not pay fees to any third-party agency or company that does not have a signed agreement with the Company.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SingleStore values individuals for their unique skills and experiences, and we’re proud to offer roles in a variety of locations across the United States. Salary is based on permissible, non-discriminatory factors such as skills, experience, and geographic location, and is just one part of our total compensation and benefits package. Certain roles are also eligible for additional rewards, including merit increases and annual bonuses. SingleStore’s base salary range for this role, $130,000 -&amp;nbsp; $175,000 USD per year&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;For candidates residing in California, please see our&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.singlestore.com/singlestore-california-recruitment-privacy-notice/&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt; California Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;. For candidates residing in the EEA, UK, and Switzerland, please see our&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.singlestore.com/recruitment-privacy/&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt; EEA, UK, and Swiss Recruitment Privacy Notice.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SingleStore is seeking a Forward Deployed Engineer (FDE) to operate at the intersection of solution architecture, technical delivery, and customer partnership. This role combines elements of a solutions architect, technical account manager, and solution engineer, with a strong emphasis on execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an FDE, you will serve as a trusted technical advisor and sounding board for customers, helping them design, implement, and scale real-time data solutions using SingleStore. You will work closely with customers to understand their business objectives, translate them into technical strategies, and drive those solutions into production. This role requires a delivery mindset, strong technical depth, and the ability to lead both strategic conversations and hands-on execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role and Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner directly with customers to understand their architecture, use cases, and business goals, and translate them into scalable technical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement end-to-end solutions integrating SingleStore into existing application and data ecosystems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead whiteboard sessions to shape ideas, define architecture, and convert concepts into technical specifications and execution plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a proactive thought partner, bringing ideas and guiding conversations rather than reacting to requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own delivery of high-impact initiatives from concept through production, ensuring successful outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide hands-on support, including troubleshooting, optimization, and applying pragmatic solutions or fixes when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with Sales, Solutions Engineering, Product, and Engineering teams to align customer needs with product capabilities and roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help customers prioritize and operationalize their data initiatives, balancing ambition with practical delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feed insights from customer engagements back into Product and Engineering to influence roadmap and improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in solution architecture, solution engineering, or technical consulting (pre-sales and/or post-sales).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong foundation in databases, distributed systems, or software engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience delivering production-grade solutions in customer-facing environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating complex systems across data pipelines, applications, and infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate ambiguous requirements into clear technical plans and drive execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with enterprise customers, particularly in financial services or high-tech environments, is highly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and organizational skills, with the ability to guide both technical and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to balance technical innovation with pragmatic delivery and realistic scoping.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Alignment with product capabilities and roadmap, ensuring solutions are both impactful and feasible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SingleStore delivers the cloud-native database with the speed and scale to power the world’s data-intensive applications. With a distributed SQL database that introduces simplicity to your data architecture by unifying transactions and analytics, SingleStore empowers digital leaders to deliver exceptional, real-time data experiences to their customers. SingleStore is venture-backed and headquartered in San Francisco with offices in Sunnyvale, Raleigh, Seattle, Boston, London, Lisbon, Bangalore, Dublin and Kyiv.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Consistent with our commitment to diversity &amp;amp; inclusion, we value individuals with the ability to work on diverse teams and with a diverse range of people.&lt;/p&gt;
